= Kronstadt and the NEP

While Central Germany was fighting, the sailors of Kronstadt rose against the Bolsheviks for soviets without communists. The Red Army crossed the ice and crushed them on 18 March. In the same days the Russian party congress ended the requisitioning of grain, let the peasants trade, and banned factions inside the party.

The *Vorwärts* writes that Lenin has brought back capitalism and shot the revolution's own sailors. Our members want to know what to say at work.

- @defend: Defend the suppression of Kronstadt without reservation.
- @explain: Explain the NEP as a retreat to save the revolution.
- @criticise: Say openly what troubles us.

@defend
subtitle: Zinoviev and Trotsky will be pleased. Not every reader will believe it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence -= 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 3);
RG.ecci('trotsky', 3);
!}

The Rote Fahne calls the Kronstadt rebels tools of the White émigrés and the French general staff.

@explain
subtitle: An honest account. Lenin will read it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
RG.ecci('lenin', 5);
!}

Thalheimer writes that the Russian workers have made a retreat in a ruined country, as an army retreats to save itself. It is the most widely read article the paper prints that spring.

@criticise
subtitle: Rosa Luxemburg's words, used against Moscow. The whole Executive will take offence.
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence += 6;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
RG.ecci('all', -4);
!}

The Rote Fahne defends the Russian revolution, and adds that freedom only for the members of one party is no freedom at all. The words are Luxemburg's. Radek asks who authorised them.
